 "note": "FR-091-AC-10 to FR-091-AC-26 (TC-980): the timestamped-event finite-window profile. Each `window` case evaluates one temporal operator at the activations named by `activate` over positions `[stamp, p]` (p is T, F, absent = valuation missing, or conflict = both values admitted). `w` is the inclusive progress watermark, `complete` the asserted completeness `through` tick or null for Incomplete, `scope` is informational (an open scope settles only by a decisive witness or counterexample). `lower` is the lower-boundary kind of a past operator. `expected.outcome` is true, false, pending or indeterminate, with `where` (position of the deciding activation), `deadline` (pending) and `reason` (indeterminate) where stated. The rules are FR-091 'established' and the possibility sets of FR-160. QSL TC-1295 rows 1 to 22, 27, 28, 31 to 33, 35 to 37, 39 and 40 are the origin (rows 23 to 26, 29, 30 and 34 are QSL entry, work and result-identity rows, or repeat row 18; row 38 is FWV-52 and FWV-73). The observations of a case may be listed in any order and are read in canonical order (stamp, order authority, key); several observations of one stamp are readings of one instant; `uncertainty` is a counter-cover uncertainty (default exact), `basis` and `support` are the settlement basis and decision-support pairs; `row` names the row. The evaluator is QSL's; QSpec's test applies the stated rule.",
